= A Reprieve from the Gallows

Following Parliament's approval of the executions of Deniz Gezmiş, Yusuf Aslan, and Hüseyin İnan, İnönü and our party have refused to abandon their efforts to save the three young men. Under İnönü's leadership, the CHP has challenged the law authorizing their executions before the Constitutional Court, arguing that Parliament failed to follow the proper constitutional procedures when approving it.

On April 6, the Constitutional Court rules in our favor and annuls the law on procedural grounds. The decision brings considerable relief to the CHP and those who have campaigned against the executions. For the first time since the death sentences were approved, it appears that our efforts may have succeeded where our opposition in Parliament had failed.

However, this victory is far from decisive. The Court has not overturned the original death sentences, and the AP, alongside the other parties supporting the executions, still commands an overwhelming parliamentary majority. There is little preventing them from introducing the legislation again and securing its approval through the proper procedures. For now, we have managed to save three young men from the gallows, but whether we can prevent their eventual execution remains to be seen...

